# Artwork is read byte for byte. The evaluator's content hash includes the
# SHA-256 of every asset a part document reads (RecordingAssets in
# crates/openbrick-part/src/eval/mod.rs), so every checkout must hold the same
# bytes, or the CLI, the playground and the golden tests disagree. Git for
# Windows with core.autocrlf on (as on the Windows CI runners) would otherwise
# check these files out with CRLF line endings. -text turns off every line-ending
# conversion for them, on checkout and on commit; diffs still show as text.
# crates/openbrick-part/tests/brand.rs checks that the brand artwork has no CR.
*.svg -text
parts/assets/** -text
